      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>Publirations.</head>
        <p>Publirations.</p>
        <p>ri 11411 TRUTH ABOUT STAMMERING.—Anyoce Interested will receive the latest information and important books on the cure, on I ,an. post free, without charge, from Ithurial, Messrs. DEACON'S, 154; Leadenhall-street, London, B.C.</p>
        <p>“HOW TO ENSURE HEALTH.”—A medical work giving Prescriptions and Instructions for the cure of all kinds of Debility : post free, two starops.—Address Dr. BARNES. 48, Lonsdale Square, Barns oury, London, N.</p>
        <p>AGOOD PLAN.—The safest, best and quickest way to make money by Stocks and Shares is fully ex- plained In Thirteenth annual edition of Explanatory Book sent post free. Full of valuable information. Address GEonoe EVANS and Co„ Stockbrokers, 24, Queen Victoria-st., London, E.C.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>FREE TO MEN.</head>
        <p>FREE TO MEN.</p>
        <p>When you are tired of taking nauseous and mysterious prescriptions and compounds, which do you nogold, but only ruin your digestive organs, write to me and I will send you a book which describes a QUICK AND CERTAIN dare tor lost strength, wasting weakness, Ste., from whatever cause arising. NO STOMACH MEDICINE, NO ELECTRIC- ITY. Sent in envoiope on receipt of two stamps for postage I A. S. TAIGA, 92-91 Great Russoll-streot London. W.C.</p>
        <p>BOOK FOR MARRIED WOMEN.</p>
        <p>The information contained in this book ought to be known by every married woman, aud it will not harm the unmarriep to read. The book is c mveniently divided into 12 fuhapters The first chapter treats of the changes at puberty, or when a girl becomes a woman. The second chapter treats of marriage from a doctor's standpoint ; points out the best age tar maniage, and who should have children and who not, and furnishes useful informAtion that one can online- fly get only from an intell gent doctor. The third chapter treats of the I marriage of blood relations; and condemns such marriages as a rule. Chapter four treqs of the signs of plegnancy. The fifth chapter tells how a woman should live during the pregnant state. The sixth chapter treats of mial.ape and bow to avoid them. The seventh chapter treats of maternal Impressions and shows that birthmarks are not due</p>
        <p>longings c n the part of the mother, but rather to her poor health. The Eighth chaptcr teaches bow to have easy confinements. Certain people believe that women should bring forth in pain and trouble, but the hygienic physician says that confinements can be made comparatively easy in certain rules are obeyed ; these rules are given. The ninth chapter treats of the proper management of confinement until the baby is born. The tenth chapter tells how to treat the mother till she is up and about again. Ilse eleventh chapter treats of sterility ; gives the main Causes of it, how these may be overcome and children result. The last chapter , treats of the " change," a most important article for all Iwomen over forty. The book is full of useful information and no b,ok Is w,itten which goes so thoroughly into matters relating to married women. Some may think too much is told ; such can scarcely be the ca.e. for knowledge is power ! and the means o attaining happiness. The book cart be had 1 from Dr. T. H. ALLINSON, 25 Box, 4, Spanish-place, ! klancheeter-square, London, W., in return for a Pof,tal Order for Is. Id.</p>
      </div>
