      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0091" n="art0091">
        <p>filo COUNTRY BUYEHR.—The enormous patronage en- joyed by Woreley's from customers all over Lane shire. Yorkshire, Cheshire, The Pottcnies. all over the North, The Midla-uls, and Wales, will prove how much is the saving effected by purchasing at Woraley's. In future carriage will be paid on all orders over £2O to any part of England and Wales. It is only fair to say that better value could not be obtained than Wors'ey's New Goods and the Second-band Furniture simply bewilders and demoralises competition. Never mind what distance) nu live from Manchester, it will pay you to visit Worsley'a; you will save quite 50 per cent.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <p>IAUTION.—Bee are of buying new London jerrybuilt fur- kj no matter how low the price is— it is dear at any price. Worsley's have second-hand reliable furniture by good makers, which will last for ages. Th.re is no disputing the fact that high-class second-hand furniture is better than new. The only fault is that sometimes the artic'e is old- fashioned. This is easily remeditd at Worsley's, they having over 50 cabinet makers at work modernising second-hand fur- niture when necessary. For instance, second-h rnd side- boards are easily modernised by having the backs raised, the plates bevelled, and the panels carved. You never need fear cracking, blistering, grub eaten, or moth eaten furniture at Worsley's. Secand-hand furniture is not troubled with these complaints. They give a written warranty for 10 years with all furnishhing orders.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0093" n="art0093">
        <p>GREAT BARGAINS IN COMPLETH HOUSES OF FUhNITURB.</p>
        <p>HOUSE OF FURNITURE FOR £2O.</p>
        <p>A capital House of Furniture is now on view, late the property of Mr. Godfrey, of Moss Side Manchester. contains complete furniture for sitting or dining-room, kitchen, bed- rooms, hall, stairs, landing, .tc. Full particulars post tree.— WORSLHY'S.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <p>HOUSES OF FURNITURE (S)COND HAND). £lO, £2O, £3O. £4O, £5O, £75, and £lOO Houses of furni- ture in stock have been considerably reduced, complete lists of which will be sent on application post free. All guaranteed for five years.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0095" n="art0095">
        <p>TMPORTANT,—The whole of the goods advertised be:ow are priced at the lowest possible figure, for prompt cash; if required by deferred payments, 10 per cent must be added.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0096" n="art0096">
        <p>THE GREATEST BARGAINS IN THE WORLD. --</p>
        <p>COMPLETE HOUSES OF FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>Lot 1. Splendid House of ,Furniture, complete, the most substantial lot in this city, and containing more for the money. The Dintng-morn has a heavy Dining-room Suite, complete, in hard grain, Levant leather, the frames beauti- fully carved in has relief ; has comfortable couch and luxuri- ously upholstered easy chairs, a heavy dining table to match. extends to dine 40, with incised early English legs on patent castors; a handsome Perian bordered carpet and rug to match, solid brass bar fender.fire brasses and dogs complete; cornice, with rings, ends and brackets ; Notting. am lace curtains ; and las:, whiah is thrown in gratis, and is in addi- tion to what any competitor could do, simply for an adver- tisement, a handsome Amerio,n walnut sideboard, in the Renaissance style, to march the dinlng-roome suite. The Bedroom Suite is solid Cyprus wood &amp;not is a suite which can be highly recommended, guaranteed for 10 years, being charged in some establishments as much ar we ask for the whole of this house of furniture; a handsome solid brass and enam oiled bedstead, wills complete fittings of mattress and bedding; there are the usual accessories for bedroom—carpets, curtains, fender, chamber ware, dm. Also Kitchen Furni- ture, consisting of the usual chairs, heavy white top table, , fender, ashpan, and top bar, floorcloth or kitchen, landing. and hall. I will pack and deliver the lot for 21} guineas, 10 per cent, extra if by deferrr d payments. Call and inspect this lot, it pulverises all competition ; if you spprotve buy, it you don't there is no harm done.—WORSLEF'S.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0097" n="art0097">
        <p>4 DISASTROUS UNHAPPY MARRIAGE.—WORSLICY offers a grand opportunity in a complete House of Furniture, just purchased in consequence of a disastrous marriage resulting In separation. The whole of the furniture was made to order, and is in splendid condition. Briefly described it consists of a fine sett of Dining-room Vurniture, having a magnificent sideboard, modern in style: handsomely carved in has relief; a suite of couch, two easy chairs and six padded hack single chairs upholstered in morocco, a massive diningtable, telescopic extension, a substantial overmantel to match, and a coal cabinet, the whole being in brown oak ; also solid brass fender, dogs, and brasses. The Drawing-room Is high-class Chippendale Furniture, contains a very pretty cabinet, a settee, two elegant easy chairs and several occas- ional chairs. a match overmantel, three occasional tables, coal cabinet and a massive solid brass fender, dogs, and fire- brasses. The Best Bedroom has a magnificent satinwood suite, wardrobe with bevelled plate-glass centre door,dressi ng table, washstand, table de null, three chairs and towel airer, , a massive brass and enamelled Persian bedstead, with spring and new hair mattresses ; besides sundries. The esecond Bed- room consists just the same articles, but is furnished in American walnut. The Hall has a splendid hatstand and hall chair. The Kitchen contains the usual requisites. The whole tonna a compact. substantial, handsome house of ' furniture, space preventing anything like an adequate des- cription. The price for the let is £122 10s. A full list, con- taining every item, will be sent post ire's. The lot will he stored tree until required upon payment of 5 p. r cent deposit. Delivered free.—WORSLRY'S, tiaythorn.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0098" n="art0098">
        <p>COMPLETE ROUSH for £250. This is a special bargAin, but would take too much space to &amp;scribe. It is suitable for a semi-detached house, con- taining dining, drawing, and three bed rooms, servants' rooms, sitting-room, kitchen, hall furniture, &amp;c., carpets, oil- cloths, linoleums ;in fact, every requisite. Full particulars on application.—WOßSLEY'S.</p>
      </div>
