        <p>THE EXAMINER, SATURDAY, JULY 27, 1895.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON v. NORTHERN SECOND ELEVENS.—The . local 2nd Eleven on Saturday paid a visit to Waterloo to , play the return fixture with the above named club. The I first meeting resulted in a win tor Northern. Besides , journeying with only nine men, Warrington were minus the services of Messrs. Fleming, Adamson, Rushworth and Silcock, whilst the home eleven placed an unexc:l3- tionally strong eleven in the field. The felling was everything that could be desired and Warrington ought to be congratulated in bringing off such a brilliant per- formance. Score :--• WARRINGTON 2ND. NORTHERN 2ND. Bibby c Birley b Lloyd 2l Elwell Rev c Hagger b Brown run out l7 Bibby Duckworth b Lioyd Crompton a Fraser b Dur.indu lbw to Bibby ...... 2 Lloyd 6 Lloyd D Duckworth 6 Unsworth b Durandu ... 3 Job b Bibby... 2 Hampson b Birley Evans not out 4 Fraser c Duckworth b 1 0 Bibby Ashton c Job b Birley ... 0 Fernie c Hampson b Kiernan b Lloyd 0 Bibby Williams (sub) b Lloyd .. 1 Morgan c Crompton b Hagger sub (run out) l7 Bibby - Birley lbw b Duck- worth Fraser run out 1 Pick not out , Extras 3 Extras 4</p>
