        <p>WARRINGTON V. NORTHERN (I.avvevooL).—The re- I turn match between these clubs was played on the Arpley enclosure on Saturday, when, despite the fact that the atmospheric conditions were against the sum• mer sport, there was a large crowd present. This was brought about no doubt by the appearance of Mr. W. G. Druce, the Cambridge University captain, who has ac- complished some remarkable achievemews for his team this season, and who has an average of 47 runs per inn- ings. The fiulding, on both sides was smart, but by far the best bowling performance was that of Mr. J. J. Crosfiuld, whose seven wickets cost 39 runs. Score and bowling analysis :</p>
