      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0130" n="art0130">
        <head>BO WLIN (1.</head>
        <p>BO WLIN (1.</p>
        <p>BOWLING MATCH AT SANKEY.—A match was played on the green attached to the Sankey Chapel House,between teams captained by Mr. R. Woods and Mr. J. Helaby (two well known Bank Quay bowlers), and resulted in a win for:Woods's team by 10 points. After the match the teams sat down to an excellent knife and fork tea provided by Mrs.Jenka, Ship Inn, Liverpool-road. Full justice having been done to the meal, the remainder of the evening was spent in a convivial manner. The fol- lowing are the scores : WOODS'S TEAM. HELSBY TEAM. R Woods 9 John Hobby ll J Wilcock J Webb J Jackson Jodeph Potter Wiliam Smith ll James Ashton James Hill ll Thomas Forster 4 H Rhodes S Jones Joseph Hammel, 5 H Kent</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0131" n="art0131">
        <head>Total 9O Total BO WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT BOWLING LEAGUE.</head>
        <p>Total 9O Total BO WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT BOWLING LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON CEMETERY HOTEL V. HORSE AND JOCKEY IST TEAMS.—These teams met on the Cemetery Green on Saturday last when the home team scored their third victory this season by 24 points. Owing to the heavy rains the green told greatly against the players. Below are the individual sgores : CEMETERY HORSE &amp; JOCKEY G Ball, jun. H Williams J Hewitt T Ellison A Allison It Roth well J D Brimelow (captain) l3 J. Hardman R Farrington 0 Ball, sen. E Taylor l5 H Dagnall 4 T Bolt m l5 J Webb (captain) l3 W °leave</p>
        <p>Total l6O Total 136 Mr. IL Bennett officiated as referee. The following is the position of clubs up to date:— Matches played. Won. Lost P'ts. Cemetery Hotel Club ' Bull's Head Club Horse and Jockey Club Red Lion Club Liberal Club LIBERAL V. CONSERVATIVE Ca.uns.—Representatives of the two local political clubs played a friendly game of bowls on Saturday afternoon on the green at the Liberal club. The Liberals gave their )pponents a cordial re- ception, and afterwards a good beating though not so severe a beating as they did a year ago, when the first of these friendly matches was played. In the doubles the visitors almost held their own, only losing by four, but in the singles they lost by 35 thus giving the Liberals a total majority of 39. The games were most pleasantly contested. The following are the scores : L13E1211, CLUB. CONSERVATIVE CLUB. Singles. Doubles. Singles. Doubles. 8 M Knowles 11 C Browne 11 T Locker 11 J Parker 11 H Williams 2 W H Hooper 11 A J Jones l5 83 Bi•linge 11 W Stephenson lO T Cooper 11 J nnings ....... ........ is 4 W Wilson 11 J Harrison 8 B Shearer lO 11 W Hill l5 11 F It Jones 11 Bradbutn 8 .7 Baker 9 Mitchell 11 Taylor . 10 I Gibson l5 11 I ongshaw 11 Albinson l3 0 S Caldwell l5 6 Haynes 8 Benson l4 113 Millington 15 11 Parr... 5 T Horrabin, jur</p>
