        <p>SPSCIAL NOTICE.—WORSLEY'S BUY, SELL, or EX- CHANGE FURNITURE to any amount; are the Oldest-established Bona Fide Brokers in Manchester. If you wish to sell your Furniture, go to Wortiley's, and save trouble and expense of auction. If you wish to buy Second-hand Furniture. go to Worsley's. There is more genuine Second- hand Furniture there than all the other dealers put together. If you wish to Exchange your Furniture, go to Worsley's, as you will be fairly and equitably denit with.</p>
        <p>WBBHLY CHAT.—Subject: Second-hand Furniture— The opening of Spring is the time for the busy house- wife to put her house in order, therefore the matter of furni- shing must be well discussed. We cannot, therefore, do better than advise a visit to Wortley's before definitely de- riding where and what to purchase. This visit cannot pos- sibly but prove remunerative, if only in experience. "The Pantheon ' being a hive of industry, it is a palatial pile of buildings close to the Central Station, having a frontage of nearly 150 feet This immense building is filled torn floor to ceiling (six storeys) with the grandest collection of High- class Second-hand Furniture In the World. This is not an exaggeration, but can be verified by ocular dernonetrat lon if you pay a visit to Manchester. Suites of Bedroom Furni- ture, for instance, by such makers as Goodall. Lamb, Ogden, !cc., original cost twin £2OO to £3OO, for from £5O to £7O ; suites, original cost £5O to £7O, for £lO to £2O. Pay a visit and see for yourself ; you can surely use your common sense, and see if Worsley's is the place as described.</p>
        <p>KTEW FURNITETEB.—AII Woreley's new furniture is their own make. Of course it is obviously impossible to sup- ply every requlrem.nt second-hand. Woral,y's have, there- fore. erected a Cabinet Works in City-road, with an immense stock of seasoned timber for the production of reliable furni- ture. livery item in the Bedding Department is new, guaran- teed pure, under minute inspection.</p>
        <p>C--- ORIPLIaIi FURNISHING ORDERS.—Worsley's cater specially for Complete Furnishing Orders, supply estimates free, and believe in the equity of supplying com- plete orders at a less ratioof profit than single articles.</p>
        <p>FIERI FACIAS. A writ of Fierl Facing has been the means of Wornley's securing the whole of the furniture of a 801 l on gentleman, and is now on view at Worsley's at an enormous sacrifice. Prices are quoted separately for each room. It sold in one lot 10 per cent. will be deduAed, but any single article may be pu based . Every art tole guaranteed for 10 years; delivered carriage paid.—lnspect ion invited. The Dining Room Is handsomely furnished In pollard oak, contains a massive suite, richly carved. upholstered in the most expensive English morocco leather, stuffed in hair- a magnificent 51t. 6in, sideboard, the Most te,utifully marked and figured wood in lingland ; a grand 12ft. dining table, heavy carved legs; a splendid heavy overmantel to match. also a high pollard oak coal cabinet; the whole originally designed and produced by Mr. Robinson, the eminent draughtsman, for nearly £4DO; our price £137. A wonderful bargain.</p>
        <p>The Drawing is a charming picture of good taste, being en- tirely Chippendale, contains, briefly, an elegant Sit. cabinet, all carved and perforated in Egyptian pediments fitted with brilliant plate-glass panels ; a recherche suite of settee, 2 easy and 6 occasional chairs, all various designs, tipholsterei in silk Genoa as desired, selection ( f tints sulmitted, the whole having been repaired for re-covering; a very beautiful over- mantel and a set of three occasional tables complete; a very fine suite, to be sold a bargain for £7O guineas ; worth £250. The Breakfast Boom is furnished in American walnut and would be acceptable in any dining room, has a 61t. sideboard of massive proportions, beautifully carved in bas relief ; a Suite of nine pieces in Oriental saddle bag+, the couch and easy chairs are large and comfortably luxurious; good heavy Dining Table, Overmantel, and Coal Cabinet. complete; the let for which theridiculously low price of £32 106. will secure a great bargain, The Bedrooms. four in number, contain magnificent furni- ture. The best bedroom Suite is one of the handsomest in Manchester, made by Henry Ogden and Sons, in remarkably handsome satinwood; cost £250. The wardrobe is worth double our price for the lot. The suite consists of the ward- robe Sit., finessing table Sit., washstand Sit., pedestal cup- board, chairs i.nd rail ; our price for quick sale £65. Magni- ficent solid bra,. Persian Bedstead, sft. stifle with spring mattress, thick hair mattress; Silk Plush and Cretonne Dra- pers ; the lot for £2O, worth £6O. The Second Bedroom contains an extraordinary Pollard Oak Bedroom Suite, by Shepperton, full suite as the best room ; wardrobe 611 ,and is honestly worth £75 ; our pace £35. The bra,s Persian bedstead, similar to the best room and completely fitted, will be sold for £l2 108. The 1 bird Be lroom contains a splendid American Walnut Bedroom Suite tor 20 guineas, exquisitely carved, full of beanty, and in agrand bargain. Brass bedstead complete as described above in the best room for £9 9s. The Youith Bedroom contains a Suite in American Ash, a full, complete suite for 10 guineas ; also a br,ss Persian bed- stead complete for £6los. The furniture as described above Is on view, and will be packed and delivered free, stored until required, and a. written warranty with everything for 10 years.</p>
